There are a lot of defensive characteristics in the game, which, at first glance, you won't be able to figure out quickly. But we're here to show you that it's much simpler than that. Let's get to the bottom of it.
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/45386108/d97bab065629b4982e5352fc461debf7930a42a3.png[/img]
There are only three main defense stats. They primarily affect the damage of certain attacks on the character. Here they are:
[list]
[*] Defense against melee attacks;
[*] Defense against ranged attacks;
[*] Defense against magic attacks.
[/list]Let's take a brief look at how these defense stats are distributed among units of different formations. Let's start with the Free Empire. Leaders have roughly the same defense against all attacks, Warriors are vulnerable to magic, and Gunners are slightly better protected against ranged attacks. Dodgers are most vulnerable to melee attacks and generally have some of the lowest defenses. Mages are vulnerable to melee and ranged attacks, but are well protected against magic. Healers' defense is balanced, but they are slightly better protected against magic. At the second rank, the difference in defense indicators is not significant and is consistent with the above principle, so we will not focus on it.

The Mountain Clans are traditionally the most survivable faction due to their high amount of health, but the distribution of defense stats is almost identical to the Free Empire, but they are distinguished by their more survivable Arrows and Dodgers. The former are equally good at close and ranged attacks, while the latter are slightly better at defending against ranged attacks.

Forest Union Warriors have excellent defense against ranged attacks and are better at holding their own against mages when compared to other Warriors. The leaders of this faction are well protected against all three types of attacks, just like the other factions. Riflemen have almost the same stats as Free Empire Riflemen, but have increased defense against magic. Dodgers are good against magic and ranged attacks, but are vulnerable in close quarters. Mages have extremely low physical defense, but good defense against magic. Healers are the same, but have slightly better defense against physical attacks than mages.

Resists, in turn, are distributed in a more diverse way. Under resistances in Odra Online we mean protection from various kinds of elemental effects. 

Available resistances:
[list]
[*] Light;
[*] Darkness;
[*] Fire;
[*] Water;
[*] Air;
[*] Earth;
[*] Nature;
[*] Alchemy.
[/list]Warriors, Riflemen, and Faction Leaders do not have resistances. Exceptions are mercenaries and Forest Union Leaders. Ents and Huorns are well protected against Nature, while Swamp Gworns are well protected against Nature and Darkness.

Forest Alliance healers are well protected from Nature. The exception is the Ovates. They partially sacrifice this resist, in exchange gaining resist from the element of earth. The Free Empire's healers are similarly well protected from light, with the Shepherd being the exception - his resistances are equally divided between light and darkness. Dwarven healers have increased resistance to alchemy. Potions Master is slightly less protected from it, but has resistance to natural effects.

Forest Alliance mages have roughly the same resistances as Healers, but one of the second ranked units sacrifices nature resistances for protection against alchemy instead of protection against earth elements. Mages of the Mountain Clans, on the other hand, have split resistances from the start. Hermits are protected from water and earth, while Storm Lords are protected from water and air. Runists, as an exception, have excellent defense against earth with no other resistances. Wizards of the Free Empire are similarly protected against fire and air. Warlocks are only protected from fire, but their resistances are impressive. Elementalists, the only mages at all, have protection from all elemental effects.

Let's not forget the Dodgers, the only non-magical class with resistances. Nymphs, Dryads, and Undines have excellent protection from nature, but Undine has a negative resistance to fire and an impressive defense against water. This means she oh-so-dislikes fire spells. Take note. The Mountain Clans' Saboteurs and Bombers are logically protected from fire, and the Engineer, sacrificing half of his fire defense, has air resistance. The mysterious Dodgers of the Free Empire have a rare defense against darkness in their arsenal. The Assassin has less resist than Shadow, but has protection against alchemy.

That's it! It's a bit long, but informative. Nevertheless, we advise you to get acquainted with the defensive indicators of units directly in the game, and develop profitable strategies there. We have only shared the patterns with you.
